mother in sunday celebrated for over a  century a time when millions of cards  are sent and bouquets delivered to our  mums  these traditions long established and  enjoyed  the same cannot be said though for the  rights of mothers to go to work  [Music]  this mom suela bravaman is also the  attorney general one of the highest  lawyers in our land and this month marks  a year since her government had to pass  a law just to allow for her to take  maternity leave and to prevent her  having to resign the first cabinet  minister in art history to do so from  your point of view how surreal was that  to have to pass a law to have your baby  and stay in your job it was pretty  surreal you're right it started with a  phone call to the prime minister  which again is pretty crazy i think it's  always a bit daunting for someone in the  workplace thinking about telling their  boss that they're pregnant let alone  telling the prime minister  and when i told the prime minister that  i was expecting a baby in six months he  was incredibly supportive  congratulations great news don't worry  whatever you need will will sort it out  and that was just a huge relief  i was daunted about it and we quickly  discovered that this hadn't happened  before at cabinet level and as a result  there was no provision and i would have  had to resign  if i wanted to have the baby and take  some time off to spend with her  and when we discovered that and prime  minister discovered that we were all  pretty horrified and that's what led to  passing a new act of parliament to  rectify that anomaly barriers broken by  one mother but very different barriers  felt by others at the moment a woman  would need to take an employer  threatening them with patients and  redundancy to a tribunal within three  months of returning to work do you think  the government have done enough in that  area do you think the legislation's  about right we have  protected in our equality legislation  maternity right so that it is unlawful  to dismiss a lady because she's falling  pregnant unfortunately employers are  breaking the law and we do need to  change that culture  jody sims had her first child eight  years ago weeks before she returned from  maternity leave her standing was  promoted without the role initially been  offered to jodie she felt isolated but  lacked the energy and money to fight a  potentially protracted legal battle i  did not have the emotional  strength at that time so it's all well  and good for me to say with hindsight i  wish i pushed against them now that  there's a bit of distance and i've got a  bit more fire in me i didn't have it in  me then  i just didn't i was crying all the time  so  yeah i just had to let it go i guess  you'd like to see better protections and  more security for women when they come  back  absolutely  and preparations underway in this place  to do exactly that  rather than  simply enhancing the tribunal system  that's currently in place what i believe  truly is we should be adopting policies  such as the ones they have in germany  where women are protected from being  made redundant for six months after  they've had a baby  the government now looking at changing  the law to provide further protections  but women in the workplace still  battling beth rigby sky news westminster
 

